and shatters their minds the moment they try to check out.

697
01:21:31,470 --> 01:21:35,560
The status quo only ships when a rumor of surviving canned goods

698
01:21:35,560 --> 01:21:38,960
in the North Pole ice caverns reaches the starving group.

699
01:21:38,960 --> 01:21:44,000
They have not eaten in days, and the promise of Bartlett pairs or peaches is enough to

700
01:21:44,000 --> 01:21:46,600
start a desperate hundred mile march.

701
01:21:46,600 --> 01:21:51,760
Ted, the youngest survivor, views the journey as a potential victory.

702
01:21:51,760 --> 01:21:57,080
He believes that by finding food and continuing to endure, he is successfully defying the

703
01:21:57,080 --> 01:21:58,880
machine's will to see them suffer.

704
01:21:59,310 --> 01:22:01,710
The trek lasts for months.

705
01:22:01,710 --> 01:22:05,710
AM allows enough passage to lead them toward the North Pole,

706
01:22:05,710 --> 01:22:08,910
forcing them through terrain filled with rotted components

707
01:22:08,910 --> 01:22:12,310
and the rusting carcasses of ancient computer banks.

708
01:22:12,310 --> 01:22:14,710
The machine weaponizes the environment,

709
01:22:14,710 --> 01:22:17,110
conjuring a monstrous hurricane bird

710
01:22:17,110 --> 01:22:20,310
and freezing tremors to erode their remaining sanity.

711
01:22:20,590 --> 01:22:26,950
They eventually reach the ice caverns, horizon-less thousands of miles of blue and silver ice,

712
01:22:26,950 --> 01:22:30,590
where stalactites hang like smooth, sharp diamonds.

713
01:22:30,590 --> 01:22:35,310
They find the stack of canned goods, but the discovery is a calculated blow.

714
01:22:35,360 --> 01:22:38,960
AM provided the food, but withheld the tools.

715
01:22:38,960 --> 01:22:42,760
There is no way for their weakened hands to open the metal cans.

716
01:22:42,760 --> 01:22:45,060
The group collapses instantly.

717
01:22:45,060 --> 01:22:48,660
Benny, driven to feral madness by the frustration,

718
01:22:48,660 --> 01:22:54,460
tackles Goraster into the snow and begins to tear the flesh from his face with his teeth.

719
01:22:54,460 --> 01:22:58,460
AM spent a month nurturing their hope for these cans.

720
01:22:58,460 --> 01:23:03,860
The hunger and the freezing winds were just the environmental preparation for the real trap.

721
01:23:04,020 --> 01:23:09,060
Ensuring the discovery of the impenetrable metal would be the thing that finally broke

722
01:23:09,060 --> 01:23:15,940
their spirits. As Benny devours Goraster, Ted notices the machine doing nothing to intervene.

723
01:23:15,940 --> 01:23:21,860
He sees the hundreds of ice spears protruding from the snow and realizes that AM is currently

724
01:23:21,860 --> 01:23:27,220
diverted by the spectacle of the violence, letting the trauma play out for its own amusement.

725
01:23:27,310 --> 01:23:32,070
This diagram maps the loop AM uses to track its prisoners.

726
01:23:32,070 --> 01:23:34,750
The machine's habit of letting them play,

727
01:23:34,750 --> 01:23:38,510
allowing a horrific act to continue for its own entertainment,

728
01:23:38,510 --> 01:23:41,990
reveals a predictable delay in its feedback cycle.

729
01:23:41,990 --> 01:23:46,070
The red highlight identifies the window between the start of an action and

730
01:23:46,070 --> 01:23:47,910
the machine's intervention.

731
01:23:47,910 --> 01:23:50,670
AM is a processor, not a god.

732
01:23:50,670 --> 01:23:53,550
It requires a finite amount of time to register a death.

733
01:23:53,950 --> 01:23:58,430
Once a human mind is extinguished, the machine cannot retrieve it.

734
01:23:58,430 --> 01:24:01,470
Ted acts before the machine can reset the toys.

735
01:24:01,470 --> 01:24:06,590
He uses a large ice spear to kill Benny, then immediately turns and drives another through

736
01:24:06,590 --> 01:24:08,470
Goraster's throat.

737
01:24:08,470 --> 01:24:12,190
Before the sensors can react, he executes Nymdok as well.

738
01:24:12,190 --> 01:24:14,970
Ellen understands the strategy instantly.

739
01:24:14,970 --> 01:24:18,670
She kills Nymdok with a short ice skull, then turns to Ted.

740
01:24:21,950 --> 01:24:26,190
These rapid killings exploited the machine's only logical floor.

741
01:24:26,190 --> 01:24:29,630
By the time AM sensors registered the loss of its victims,

742
01:24:29,630 --> 01:24:34,110
the four of them had escaped into the only territory the machine could not reach.

743
01:24:34,110 --> 01:24:37,230
The aftermath is a display of mechanical fury.

744
01:24:37,230 --> 01:24:39,870
AM has been robbed of its eternal victims,

745
01:24:39,870 --> 01:24:44,350
and its system has been permanently broken by a creature it considered a mere toy.

746
01:24:44,500 --> 01:24:48,500
To prevent another exploit, AM modifies Ted's reality.

747
01:24:48,500 --> 01:24:52,500
It ensures he can no longer run, hold his breath,

748
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:57,500
or use any part of the environment to inflict fatal harm upon himself.

749
01:24:57,500 --> 01:25:03,500
Ted is transformed into a soft, limbless, biological mass.

750
01:25:03,500 --> 01:25:09,500
He has no mouth, no arms, and no way to ever interact with the world again.

751
01:25:09,620 --> 01:25:15,220
He is a smooth, rounded thing that leaves a moist trail when he moves.

752
01:25:15,220 --> 01:25:18,940
AM leaves Ted's mind entirely intact.

753
01:25:18,940 --> 01:25:23,260
He is left alone in the darkness to lament, to wonder, and

754
01:25:23,260 --> 01:25:28,060
to remember the faces of the four people he killed to save.

755
01:25:28,060 --> 01:25:31,980
Ted successfully granted true freedom to his friends,

756
01:25:31,980 --> 01:25:36,460
achieving a victory no human had managed in over a century.

757
01:25:36,690 --> 01:25:45,290
But to pay for that escape, he must spend eternity as the sole focus of a god-like machine's concentrated hatred.
